19277524,2026-02-05,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Communication tactics,"You told them to stop contacting you, but they keep trying","This debt collector sent me a notice stating that it had acquired a purported debt allegedly belonging to me. The notice advised that I had the right to request validation of the debt. Shortly after receiving their letter, I mailed a written request for debt verification to the address provided by the company. The letter was sent via certified mail. In that correspondence, I also requested that the company refrain from reporting the alleged debt to any credit reporting agencies until proper verification was provided, and that all future communication be conducted by mail only. 

