19782692,2026-02-25,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers",Confusing or misleading advertising about the credit card,"I participated in two promotional balance transfer offers from Citibank. The first one I signed up for was 0 % interest and expired on XX/XX/XXXXXXXX/2026. The other one was for 1.99 %, had a fixed monthly fee and expired on XXXX/2027. I originally made a large payment intending it to go agains the balance that expired earlier and was told that the lower balance always gets first. This was very upsetting as I was trying to pay it off before expiration but understanding according to the guidelines the provided me which is all payments go to the lower interest rate. I was very concerned about the rate that would occur after the 0 % interest rate expired which was 22.99 % so I saved every month so I could pay that off. My statement dated ending XXXX  XXXX, 2026 and I logged into the account the day after it had ended and viewed the statement. It showed my promotional balance of {$7500.00} and said balance transfer rated expired XX/XX/XXXXXXXX/2026. The statement had a due date of XX/XX/XXXXXXXX2026. I didn't want to accrue any unnecessary interest so made a payment in full for that balance of {$7500.00}. The other balance transfer offer had a balance of {$8600.00}. They also pulled the minimum payment required for the other loan on XX/XX/XXXXXXXX2026. I received my next statement and they showed my entire payment of {$7500.00} posted to to the balance transfer offer of 1.99 % plus the additional payment of {$170.00} was posted to that balance. I was charged {$140.00} in interest on balance transfer 1. I called Citibank on XX/XX/XXXX referring to my payment made on XX/XX/XXXX and that it should have been applied to the 22.99 % interest and they opened a case. I did not hear back from them and called them on XX/XX/XXXX and they stated my case was closed and my payment would not be reallocated because the system still saw my rate as 0 % on the date of XXXX XXXX,XX/XX/XXXX2026 and had not attached the new rate yet. They offered that I could apply for another balance transfer offer for 0 % by paying 5 % transfer fee in order to pay off the new balance at the higher rate. Their own statement tells me my rate has expired. I am making a payment after that expiration date. My payment should go to the new rate. If they are applying the payment made on XX/XX/XXXX and arguing that it was the lower interest then why are they pulling another payment on XXXX/XXXX/XXXX for minimum payment due on the other balance transfer. They are unwilling to reallocate my payment and continue to charge me 22.99 % interest on my balance and only solution is for me to pay them more money on another balance transfer offer.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",CO,811XX,,Web,2026-02-25,Closed with explanation,Yes
